4025413,imgsize-882302.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Teen Uses Cancer Game: Daniel Zhang turns Tumor Tactics into learning tool; reaches 1,500 K-8 students]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133994895.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an innovative step, a San Diego teenager named Daniel Zhang crafted Tumor Tactics, an educational game designed to demystify cancer for young minds. Motivated by his grandmother's battle with the illness, Daniel aims to make intricate cancer biology accessible to children. His project has garnered funding and will be showcased at the United Nations Science Summit, alongside his role in STEAMLabs International, where he promotes STEM and arts education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-daniel-zhang-the-17-year-old-san-diego-student-who-lost-his-grandmother-to-cancer-at-nine-then-built-a-72-card-cancer-game-reaching-1500-children/articleshow/133994895.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-daniel-zhang-the-17-year-old-san-diego-student-who-lost-his-grandmother-to-cancer-at-nine-then-built-a-72-card-cancer-game-reaching-1500-children/articleshow/133994895.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-11T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133994931,imgsize-956745.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wisconsin’s Apostle Islands Could Become a National Park Under New Proposal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133973138.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wisconsins-apostle-islands-have-been-a-national-lakeshore-since-1970-a-new-proposal-would-tu