ey-red-sea-port-in-blow-to-saudi-forces/articleshow/134015236.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T20:49:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134017353,imgsize-115441.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US resumes immigrant visa processing for Hungary, Poland while wider pause continues: What it means]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134016220.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-resumes-immigrant-visa-processing-for-hungary-poland-while-wider-pause-continues-what-it-means/articleshow/134016220.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-resumes-immigrant-visa-processing-for-hungary-poland-while-wider-pause-continues-what-it-means/articleshow/134016220.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T20:36:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134016488,imgsize-42784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hong Kong cattle DNA reveals how livestock adapted to island life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133997784.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/cattle-were-left-behind-in-hong-kong-centuries-ago-a-2026-genome-study-found-their-dna-holds-a-record-of-how-livestock-adapted-to-island-life/articleshow/133997784.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/cattle-were-left-behind-in-hong-kong-centuries-ago-a-2026-genome-study-found-their-dna-holds-a-record-of-how-livestock-adapted-to-island-life/articleshow/133997784.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T14:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133997784,imgsize-174685.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The US had just two 500-foot smokestacks in 1970 and more than 180 by 1985 to dilute pollution]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014938.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an effort to mitigate local air pollution, American power companies constructed towering smokestacks, effectively releasing sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides into higher winds. Unfortunately, this practice contributed to acid rain, harming ecosystems throughout North America. In response, Congress revised the Clean Air Act to restrict the use of tall stacks and improve emission control by emphasizing source capture instead.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-had-just-two-500-foot-smokestacks-in-1970-and-more-than-180-by-1985-to-dilute-local-pollution-the-taller-stacks-sent-emissions-farther-downwind-and-helped-spread-acid-rain/articleshow/134014938.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-had-just-two-500-foot-smokestacks-in-1970-and-more-than-180-by-1985-to-dilute-local-pollution-the-taller-stacks-sent-emissions-farther-downwind-and-helped-spread-acid-rain/articleshow/134014938.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:59:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134015120,imgsize-46957.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Jersey built a massive seawall to protect a highway and beach houses from erosion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014563.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In New Jersey, the construction of a seawall has safeguarded properties but has inadvertently resulted in the disappearance of the sandy shoreline. The energy from waves is redirected downwards, which has stripped away sand and left no beach visible even during low tide. This hard engineering tactic disrupts the natural flow of sand and hinders the migration of barrier islands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-built-a-massive-seawall-to-protect-a-highway-and-beach-houses-from-erosion-usgs-says-the-wall-concentrated-wave-energy-until-the-beach-it-was-meant-to-defend-disappeared-completely/articleshow/134014563.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-built-a-massive-seawall-to-protect-a-highway-and-beach-houses-from-erosion-usgs-says-the-wall-concentrated-wave-energy-until-the-beach-it-was-meant-to-defend-disappeared-completely/articleshow/134014563.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:52:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014806,imgsize-160554.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gwyneth Paltrow turned $4.9 million Montecito property into 14,000-sq-ft estate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014011.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Gwyneth Paltrow bought about 2.4 acres in Montecito for $4.9 million in 2016, razed the existing structures and embarked on a ground-up project that took about six years. The result was a roughly 14,000-square-foot home powered by solar energy and equipped with a graywater system.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-gwyneth-paltrow-bought-2-4-acres-in-montecito-for-4-9-million-during-a-historic-drought-over-a-6-year-journey-she-razed-two-old-homes-and-built-a-14000-sq-ft-estate-with-more-than-60-solar-panels-and-a-graywater-system/articleshow/134014011.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-gwyneth-paltrow-bought-2-4-acres-in-montecito-for-4-9-million-during-a-historic-drought-over-a-6-year-journey-she-razed-two-old-homes-and-built-a-14000-sq-ft-estate-with-more-than-60-solar-panels-and-a-graywater-system/articleshow/134014011.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:44:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014056,imgsize-129499.cms"/></item></channel></rss>